From 17cfa685624a7da889d1248a651f8d53a2a1fa9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:41:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] patch 6: whm-backend DPP fixes, NBAPI onboarding config,
 and GW profile-3 signaling

Fixes and NBAPI plumbing found while validating the previous 5 patches on
the whm (pwhm/ambiorix) platform:

- bpl_running_mode.{h,cpp} (new): tracks whether this BPL instance is
  linked into beerocks_agent or beerocks_controller, set once at startup
  in each main().
- bpl_cfg.h/cfg backends: new cfg_set_onboarding_type()/
  cfg_set_1905_security_enabled() setters, wired from NBAPI.
- controller.odl.in/agent.odl.in, on_action.cpp, db.h/db.cpp: expose
  Configuration.OnboardingType (WSC|DPP) and
  Configuration.LinkEncryptionEnable on both Controller and Agent, plus a
  new persistent Network.ProvisionDPP[] table (Alias/DPPURI) that mirrors
  its rows into the Configurator's file-backed DPP URI cache via
  DppConfiguratorTask::sync_provisioned_uris().
- controller.cpp/.h: only promotes an agent to Profile-3/DPP when the
  controller's own onboardingtype is DPP (controller_supports_dpp),
  falling back to Profile-1 otherwise; clears stale
  dpp_security_required/pmk_1905_valid/tk_1905_installed state (and
  uninstalls the transport key) when an agent re-Searches without a Chirp
  TLV, so it isn't locked out of the plaintext WSC path after switching
  back from DPP; drops noisy per-CMDU dispatch logging.
- dpp_configurator_task.h: shortens SESSION_TIMEOUT_SEC 30s -> 10s; adds
  get_dpp_configurator_task() accessor on Controller.
- agent_db.h/topology_task.cpp: adds local_controller_dpp_capable so a
  combined Controller+Agent (GW), whose co-located agent always onboards
  itself via WSC, can still report Multi-AP Profile-3 in its own Topology
  Response based on its local controller's DPP capability rather than its
  own (always-WSC) onboarding state.
- ap_wlan_hal_whm.cpp/slave_wlan_hal_whm.cpp: drop the now-unnecessary
  per-VAP DPP.RelayController write; rename the relay object/params to
  WiFi.DPPRelay./RelayEnable to match the current whm datamodel, and add
  diagnostic logging around dpp_send_frame()/SendDppFrame failures.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
